  "description": "The package is designed to use services, assistants, models, and other components related to network technologies. \n        It includes tools for creating an Http-client, asynchronous execution POST-method, and auxiliary classes for performing routine tasks. \n        This package simplifies development by allowing developers to focus on business logic rather than technical details. \n        In the future, it is planned to add additional general-purpose classes and interfaces to enhance functionality.",
